      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/02/new-york-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-kathy-hochul",
      "description": "<p>Kathy Hochul briefs journalists with state attorney general Letitia James, who will be taking over the entire case</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/01/letitia-james-cornell-gang-rape\">Letitia James appointed special prosecutor in alleged gang-rape at Cornell</a></p></li></ul><p>Kathy Hochul, New York’s governor, said on Friday that she would “ensure” that all the facts of the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/28/cornell-fraternity-investigation-alleged-gang-rape\">alleged gang-rape</a> at a fraternity house at Cornell University “are brought into the light”, while harshly criticizing the elite institution for how it handled the 2024 case.</p><p>Hochul, a Democrat, said the woman in the case, was “failed” by people obligated to protect her, including the police and the county prosecutor.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/02/new-york-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-kathy-hochul\">Continue reading...</a>",
